SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    0 / number of array dimensions                     EXTEND  =                    T                                                  END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'BINTABLE'           / binary table extension                         BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     NAXIS1  =                  236 / length of dimension 1                          NAXIS2  =               108030 / length of dimension 2                          PCOUNT  =                    0 / number of group parameters                     GCOUNT  =                    1 / number of groups                               TFIELDS =                   21 / number of table fields                         TTYPE1  = 'l       '           / Galactic longitude of star                     TFORM1  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE2  = 'b       '           / Galactic latitude of star                      TFORM2  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE3  = 'mag     '           / PS1(g,r,i,z,y), 2MASS(J,H,K), & WISE(W1,W2) magTFORM3  = '10E     '                                                            TDIM3   = '(10)    '                                                            TTYPE4  = 'mag_err '           / Uncertainties in mag                           TFORM4  = '10E     '                                                            TDIM4   = '(10)    '                                                            TTYPE5  = 'mag_int '           / Intrinsic mag from APOGEE stellar parameters   TFORM5  = '10E     '                                                            TDIM5   = '(10)    '                                                            TTYPE6  = 'ebv     '           / E(B-V) to star                                 TFORM6  = 'E       '                                                            TTYPE7  = 'ebv_err '           / Uncertainties in ebv                           TFORM7  = 'E       '                                                            TTYPE8  = 'rv      '           / R(V) to star                                   TFORM8  = 'E       '                                                            TTYPE9  = 'rv_err  '           / Uncertainties in rv                            TFORM9  = 'E       '                                                            TTYPE10 = 'x       '           / Extinction curve parameter x to star           TFORM10 = 'E       '                                                            TTYPE11 = 'p       '           / Parallax of star from Gaia early data release 3TFORM11 = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE12 = 'p_err   '           / Uncertainties in p                             TFORM12 = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE13 = 'flags   '           / Bit mask of flags, see description below       TFORM13 = 'J       '                                                            TTYPE14 = 'cloud_ID'           / ID for molecular clouds, see CLOUD_0-CLOUD_10  TFORM14 = 'J       '                                                            TTYPE15 = 'T       '           / Planck dust equilibrium temperature to star    TFORM15 = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE16 = 'T_err   '           / Uncertainties in T                             TFORM16 = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE17 = 'beta    '           / Planck dust emission spectral index to star    TFORM17 = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE18 = 'beta_err'           / Uncertainties in beta                          TFORM18 = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE19 = 'tau     '           / Planck optical depth at 353GHz to star         TFORM19 = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE20 = 'tau_err '           / Uncertainties in tau                           TFORM20 = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE21 = 'radiance'           / Planck integrated emission to star             TFORM21 = 'D       '                                                            CLOUD_0 = 'Not used in MC analysis'                                             CLOUD_1 = 'Taurus  '                                                            CLOUD_2 = 'Perseus '                                                            CLOUD_3 = 'Orion A '                                                            CLOUD_4 = 'Orion B '                                                            CLOUD_5 = 'Monoceros'                                                           CLOUD_6 = 'NGC 2264'                                                            CLOUD_7 = 'Ophiuchus'                                                           CLOUD_8 = 'California'                                                          CLOUD_9 = 'NGC 1579'                                                            CLOUD_10= 'Rosette '                                                                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~            This file contains E(B-V) and R(V) values for APOGEE targets from SDSS          DR17 using the methods outlined in Hobson-Ritz et al (2026). These              values are prior to the transformation into the Zhang et al (2025)              scaling. To convert the R(V) values to that scaling, multiply the rv            column by 0.974 and subtract 0.197. The 1 sigma errors for R(V) are the         R(V) 1 sigma error due to photometric errors taken in quadrature                with 0.1.                                                                                                                                                       Flags:                                                                          0: ebv < 0.3, rv will be particularly uncertainty                               1: photometry with uncertainty < 0.2 available in < 7 bands;                    use with caution                                                                2: photometry with uncertainty < 0.2 available in < 9 bands                     3: uncertainty in g, r, or W2 photometry > 0.2, rv will be unreliable           4: significant uncertainty in rv, use with caution                      END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             